102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (In October 2025, Digital Rights Watch partnered with Essential Media to run a national event series exploring how democracy can survive the rise of AI. The tour visited Adelaide, Perth, Brisbane, Sydney and Melbourne, featuring expert panels and performances from local creatives. The events drew diverse audiences united by a shared curiosity about AI and its social impact. To watch or listen to recordings of these events, check out the resources tab at the bottom of this report.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (Digital Rights Watch set out to understand how these audiences think about the intersection of AI and democracy. We collected and analysed the comments shared at each event, and this report summarises the key themes that emerged. Our aim is to provide insight into how people actively engaged with AI are conceptualising its risks, possibilities, and democratic implications.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
