161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (30% of responses referred to regulation. Melbourne \(40%\) and Perth \(38%\) had the highest rates of regulation support, followed by Brisbane \(31%\) and Adelaide \(27%\). Despite Sydney having the lowest levels of regulation support \(21%\) out of all the event locations, regulation was still the most popular suggestion there. This made regulation the most popular theme across all states, suggesting a strong belief among participants that AI regulation will benefit democracy. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (The majority of regulation-focused responses were general in their reference to regulation, but others pinpointed particular areas requiring regulation. These areas include regulating AI use in schools, regulating media, and international regulation. However, privacy regulation was the most popular specific regulation request, representing 6% of all regulation comments. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
